(Plain layout: this test's golden file is a full dump of one generated
 program, and its job is to record what the generator WRITES. Under the
 random layout that dump is a wall of drawn whitespace, unreadable as a
 record and churning on any change to the pass. Layout has its own gate
 in 270_layout, and its determinism is covered by 220_determinism, which
 runs on the default random layout.)
'gen set layout' of "plain".

'gen program' of 42 and 12.
a text called t1 is 'gen text'.
Print "--- seed 42 ---".
Print t1.

'gen program' of 42 and 12.
a text called t2 is 'gen text'.
Print "reproducible: {t1 is equal to t2}".